// expect: refuse E_EffectUnhandled
// The library's own clock pins its instance with no text of its own: its
// config parameter shares its name with Sample's, so `sample_at(48000)`
// serves Sample(48000), a stage written for 44.1 kHz passes it, and with no
// clock at its rate the root refuses, proposing `~> sample_at(44100)`. On
// boot 342695ce the install absorbed every instance of Sample by its name,
// and the stage read 48000 as its rate.
import dsp/clock

fn rate44() with Sample(44100) = sample_rate()

fn main() = rate44() - 44090 ~> sample_at(48000)
